    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, let's see. I need to add 723,460 and 189,100. Hmm. Let me start by writing them down one under the other to align the digits properly.\n\nSo:\n\n  723,460\n+ 189,100\n-----------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 0 and 0. Adding them gives 0. So the ones place of the sum is 0.\n\nNext, the tens place. The digits are 6 and 0. 6 + 0 is 6. So the tens place is 6.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. Here we have 4 and 1. 4 + 1 equals 5. So that's 5 in the hundreds place.\n\nNow the thousands place. The digits are 3 and 9. 3 + 9 is 12. Oh, wait, that's two digits. So I write down 2 in the thousands place and carry over 1 to the next digit.\n\nNext is the ten-thousands place. We have 2 and 8. But don't forget the carry-over. So 2 + 8 is 10, plus the 1 carried over makes 11. So we put 1 in the ten-thousands place and carry over another 1.\n\nMoving to the hundred-thousands place. The digits are 7 and 1. Adding them gives 8, plus the carried-over 1 makes 9. So that's 9 in the hundred-thousands place.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 912,560. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carrying over.\n\n723,460\n+189,100\n= ?\n\nStarting from the right:\n0+0=0\n6+0=6\n4+1=5\n3+9=12 (carry 1)\n2+8=10 +1=11 (carry 1)\n7+1=8 +1=9\n\nYes, that adds up to 912,560. Looks correct!",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_answer": "912560",
