8 \u2192 8, no carryover.\n\nThousands: 0 + 9 = 9 \u2192 9, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands: 1 + 9 = 10 \u2192 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands: 3 + 9 = 12 + 1 (carryover) = 13 \u2192 3, carryover 1.\n\nThen, since we're at the highest digit, we add that carryover as a new digit to the left: 1.\n\nSo the sum is 1,309,801. Let me verify this with another method. Maybe by breaking down the numbers:\n\n310,609 is 300,000 + 10,000 + 600 + 9.\n\n999,192 is 900,000 + 90,000 + 9,000 + 100 + 90 + 2.\n\nAdding them:\n\n300,000 + 900,000 = 1,200,000\n\n10,000 + 90,000 = 100,000\n\n0 + 9,000 = 9,000\n\n600 + 100 = 700\n\n0 + 90 = 90\n\n9 + 2 = 11\n\nNow sum all these: 1,200,000 + 100,000 = 1,300,000\n\n1,300,000 + 9,000 = 1,309,000\n\n1,309,000 + 700 = 1,309,700\n\n1,309,700 + 90 = 1,309,790\n\n1,309,790 + 11 = 1,309,801. Yep, same result. So the answer should be 1,309,801.",
