down 7. Carry-over 0.\n\nTens place: 2 + 1 = 3. Write 3. Carry-over 0.\n\nHundreds place: 1 + 6 = 7. Write 7. Carry-over 0.\n\nThousands place: 5 + 2 = 7. Write 7. Carry-over 0.\n\nTen-thousands place: 2 + 4 = 6. Write 6. Carry-over 0.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 6 + 5 = 11. Here, we write down 1 and carry over 1 to the next higher place (millions). Since there are no more digits, the carry-over 1 becomes the millions digit.\n\nSo putting it all together, the sum is 1,167,737. Let me verify by adding:\n\n625,126 + 542,611.\n\nLet's compute 625,000 + 542,000 = 1,167,000.\n\nThen 126 + 611 = 737.\n\nAdding those together: 1,167,000 + 737 = 1,167,737. Yep, that matches. So the final answer should be 1,167,737.",
